+// RSXMemoryTiling.glsl do_memory_op and its CPU port Common/tiled_dma_copy.hpp: the offset from the tile base of the
+// texel at (row, col) of a linear region inside an RSX tile, operator for operator. The bank distribution table
+// { 0, 1, 2, 3, 2, 3, 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 0, 3, 0, 1, 2 } is written as arithmetic (row r of the table adds the 2-bit reversal
+// of r to the column, modulo 4), so that the code holds no array. m4_detile_source is the decoder's gather: for byte
+// linear_byte of the packed linear image (rows image_pitch bytes apart), the byte of the tiled data (which starts
+// tile_rw_offset bytes after the tile base and is tiled_length bytes long) it comes from: the texel's tiled offset plus
